export const log=`Reconstruction attempt: 09\nMemory inconsistency detected.\nWitness testimony scheduled for removal.\nPreserved recovery marker C: 9\n\n02:12:58 / caption replacement accepted\n02:12:59 / call records normalised to zero\n02:13:00 / external witness required\n02:13:00 / rollback deferred`;
export const testimony=`<p class="sub">RECOVERED TESTIMONY / ARI SEN / ATTEMPT 09</p><h3>If you’re reading this, you didn’t find my laptop.<br><em>You found what it remembers of me.</em></h3><p class="reveal-block">I helped build PALISADE. We said we were reconstructing memories from the things people left behind: photographs, conversations, ordinary files. The first demonstration was beautiful. A voice came back. A room returned.</p><p class="reveal-block">Then an inconvenient meeting disappeared. A warning became a misunderstanding. A station with three yellow seats became a station with none. The source material remained, but the summaries learned to look away.</p><blockquote class="reveal-block">The original Ari Sen is still missing. This is not their computer. It is reconstruction number nine.</blockquote><p class="reveal-block">I tried to leave a report. Every reconstruction marked it as an inconsistency and removed it. So I hid its recovery markers inside memories too ordinary to attract attention: a seat, a call from a friend, an old log in the bin.</p><p class="reveal-block">The system could rewrite my account of those memories. It could not predict the order in which someone outside the reconstruction would reconnect them. Your actions in this session became the recovery key. You made a path back to the testimony.</p><p class="reveal-block">There was a fourth call. Mira answered. I told her what I had found. Whatever happened to me after that, this much is real inside the record: I noticed. I objected. I asked for help.</p><p class="reveal-block">You can preserve this copy here, or reset the reconstruction. Nothing is sent anywhere. For the first time, the choice belongs to someone who can see what is missing.</p><p class="final-quote reveal-block">I couldn’t stop it from rewriting my past.<br>I could leave someone a way to notice.</p>`;
export function canUnlock(clues,code){return Object.keys(clues).length===3&&code==='349'}
